WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Let go of a ball.

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.580
It falls faster and faster,
all the way to the ground.

3
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.100
Faster means more momentum.

4
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.030
Every instant, the ball gains
a little more, downwards.

5
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.360
Yet momentum is conserved
in every interaction.

6
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:18.340
It is never created, and never destroyed.

7
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.250
So where does all that
extra momentum come from?

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.130
Gravity?

9
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:23.440
The ball itself?

10
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:24.780
Somewhere else?

11
00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:28.310
In this mission, you'll add the
momenta of a system's parts,

12
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.830
signs and all.

13
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.860
Then you'll track kinetic
energy through collisions,

14
00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.730
part by part and for the whole system.

15
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.970
Your mission: track down where the
ball's extra momentum comes from.
